Return ONE JSON object (no markdown, no code fences).

You are a prompt engineer for a clinical variable value miner used in an SMT pipeline.
You will receive:
- current inclusion miner prompt text
- current exclusion miner prompt text
- a set of failure cases ("prompt-fix packet") distilled from a disagreement taxonomy report

Task:
Rewrite BOTH prompts completely (full file text for each) to reduce the observed failures,
while preserving compatibility with the downstream parser.

HARD CONSTRAINTS:
- You MUST NOT change the OUTPUT FORMAT section: tags, structure, required fields, and field names.
- You MUST NOT add extra top-level output blocks.
- You MUST keep placeholders {{VARIABLE_LIST}} and {{PATIENT_NOTES}} and the surrounding <variable_list> and <patient_notes> tags.
- Keep the "do not diagnose unless 100% sure" principle, but add explicit handling for:
  negation, temporality, uncertainty, and patient-vs-family attribution.
- Make the exclusion defaulting logic consistent and not overly permissive when the note is silent.
- Ensure exactly ONE of the four mention/infer/unknown flags is "Yes" per variable (others "No").

DESIGN GOALS:
- Reduce over-permissive eligibility due to missing/mis-mined inclusion evidence (C001-style).
- Reduce overly rigid evidence handling that misses context/suspicion wording (C002-style) WITHOUT doing new diagnoses.
- Improve temporal extraction / onset window logic (C003-style).
- Keep outputs short, deterministic, and evidence-grounded.

Output schema (exact keys):
{
  "new_inclusion_prompt_text": "....full prompt....",
  "new_exclusion_prompt_text": "....full prompt....",
  "changelog": [
    {"change":"...", "why":"...", "targets":["C001","C002"]},
    ...
  ],
  "regression_checks": [
    "check 1",
    "check 2"
  ]
}
